Hanumān invites Rāma to enter delightful cave city --- Rāma refuses city entry for fourteen-year exile vow --- Rāma orders crowning Sugrīva and Aṅgada heir --- Rāma orders waiting autumn rains for Rāvaṇa killing --- Sugrīva enters Kiṣkindhā welcomed by thousands --- Subjects bow as friends crown Sugrīva like Indra --- Priests gather umbrella jewels herbs offerings maidens --- Waters brought from rivers oceans in gold pots --- Gaja Hanumān Jāmbavān Nala anoint Sugrīva Vedic rite --- Sugrīva crowns Aṅgada heir and reports to Rāma regaining Rumā
